#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Programmer's Guide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to use &kugar; for reporting in your own programs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several ways to use &kugar;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a temporary file and fill it with data, organized according to the "
"<link linkend=\"kugardata-dtd\">KugarData Document Type Definition</link>. "
"Then call the <command>kugar</command> shell command ( <cmdsynopsis> "
"<command>kugar</command> <group> <option>-d <replaceable>Kugar data file</"
"replaceable></option> </group> <group> <option>-r <replaceable>Kugar "
"template file</replaceable></option> </group> </cmdsynopsis> ) to preview "
"and print the report. See <link linkend=\"prog-using-for-preview\">Using "
"&kugar; shell for previewing reports</link> for a detailed description."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use &kugar; directly in the application's code. See <link linkend=\"prog-"
"using-widget\">Using &kugar; classes for reporting</link> for a detailed "
"description."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a &Qt; designer plugin, use it to build the application &GUI; in the "
"designer and link it to the program dynamically. See <link linkend=\"prog-"
"designer-plugin\">Creating a &Qt; designer plugin</link> for a detailed "
"description."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last two ways are acceptable for &Qt; and &kde; developers; but &kugar; "
"is designed to be a report generator, independent from a programming "
"language and/or <acronym>IDE</acronym>. It uses &XML; format for describing "
"report templates and data files. So any program can produce output in "
"&kugar; data file format as described in <link linkend=\"kugardata-dtd"
"\">KugarData <acronym>DTD</acronym></link> or even a report template file "
"format (see <link linkend=\"template-dtd\">KugarTemplate <acronym>DTD</"
"acronym></link>). &kugar; shell (report viewer) can be used to preview and "
"print the generated report."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kugar; shell for previewing reports"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "The way to create and preview (print) a report is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a report template file with &kudesigner;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a data file with column values for detail bands of the report. Use "
"<link linkend=\"kugardata-dtd\">KugarData <acronym>DTD</acronym></link> to "
"produce correct data files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Run &kugar; shell to preview and print a report. For example, to do this, in "
"C or C++ languages call:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: progguide.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>system(<option>\"kugar -r <replaceable>template_file.ktf</"
"replaceable>-d <replaceable>data_file.kdf</replaceable>\"</option>)</"
"function>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Don't forget to include <filename class=\"headerfile\">stdlib.h</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kugar; classes for reporting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kugar; library includes two widgets for use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <classname>KReportViewer</classname> class is designed for &kde; "
"developers. It supports a &kde; printing system and &UNIX; localization via "
"<function>i18n()</function> calls."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <classname>MReportViewer</classname> class is designed for &Qt; "
"developers and provides real crossplatforming. It can be used not only on "
"&UNIX; platforms, but also on &Windows; and &MacOS;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to build a program that uses the &kugar; library, it should be "
"linked with <filename>libkugar.so</filename> shared library, which is "
"provided with the &kugar; distribution on all &UNIX; platforms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Include files are <filename>kugarqt.h</filename> and <filename>kugar.h</"
"filename> for &Qt; and &kde; programs respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a detailed example of how &kugar; classes can be used, look in the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/shell</filename> folder in the &kugar; "
"sources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<classname>MReportViewer</classname> (and <classname>KReportViewer</"
"classname> too) contains several public methods that can be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcdef
#: progguide.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "void <function>renderReport</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Renders the report onto a screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcdef
#: progguide.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "void <function>printReport</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Calls the print dialog to print the report."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcdef
#: progguide.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "void <function>clearReport</function>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clears the report on a screen and frees report data. Call this before "
"opening the new report."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcprototype
#: progguide.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<funcdef>bool <function>setReportData</function></funcdef> <paramdef>const "
"QString &amp;<parameter>data_file_name</parameter></paramdef>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sets report data from <replaceable>data_file_name</replaceable> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcprototype
#: progguide.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<funcdef>bool <function>setReportData</function></funcdef> <paramdef>const "
"QIODevice &amp;<parameter>data_io_device</parameter></paramdef>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets report data from <replaceable>data_io_device</replaceable> file. IO "
"device can be any successor of the <classname>QIODevice</classname> class. "
"For example, to fetch records directly from the database, create a "
"<classname>QIODevice</classname> successor and redefine all necessary "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcprototype
#: progguide.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<funcdef>bool <function>setReportTemplate</function></funcdef> "
"<paramdef>const QString &amp;<parameter>template_file_name</parameter></"
"paramdef>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets report template from <replaceable>template_file_name</replaceable> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcprototype
#: progguide.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<funcdef>bool <function>setReportTemplate</function></funcdef> "
"<paramdef>const QIODevice &amp;<parameter>template_io_device</parameter></"
"paramdef>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: funcsynopsisinfo
#: progguide.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets report template from <replaceable>template_io_device</replaceable> "
"file. IO device can be any successor of the <classname>QIODevice</classname> "
"class. For example, to obtain a report template from network storage or "
"database, create a QIODevice successor and redefine all necessary "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating &Qt; designer plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the example code of how a designer plugin is created. The code below "
"creates a plugin for a &kde; <classname>KReportViewer</classname> widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a &Qt; widget is desired, replace <classname>KReportViewer</classname> "
"with <classname>MReportViewer</classname> and <filename>kugar.h</filename> "
"with <filename>kugarqt.h</filename> in the plugin code."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: progguide.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugin usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The designer plugin will allow the usage of &Qt; Designer to place a "
"<classname>KReportViewer</classname> widget onto a window and preview it "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Programs that make use of this plugin must be linked dynamically with it. "
"The corresponding library is called <filename>libkugar_plugin.so</filename>. "
"Widgets or dialogs that include <classname>KReportViewer</classname> widget "
"must include &lt;kugar.h&gt; in implementation and have a forward "
"declaration of <classname>class KReportViewer</classname>. Includes can be "
"done with &Qt; Designer's Object Explorer (Source tab)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: progguide.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "To build the plugin run:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: progguide.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>qmake</command> <arg>kugar_plugin.pro</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: progguide.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "make"
msgstr ""

